               <t:note>
                  <t:date type="foundation" notBefore="1314" notAfter="1344">1314-44</t:date>
                  <t:desc type="foundation">During the reign of King <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS1854Amdase">ʿAmda Ṣǝyon I</t:persName> (r. <t:date>1314-1344</t:date>). According to local tradition the
                     monastery was founded by monk <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS12541YamanaAb">Yamāna ʾAb</t:persName>, under King <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS1854Amdase">ʿAmda Ṣǝyon I</t:persName>.</t:desc>
                  <t:ab type="history">Gadām. At least 25 monks live in the community; there is a  well-established church school. 
                     A more recent church dedicated to <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS9162TaklaHa">Takla Haymanot</t:persName>, associated with the monastery, is located in the vicinity.
</t:ab>
                  
                  <t:ab type="tabot">
                     <t:measure quantity="6"/>  Tābots (6?): <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6819Mary#Zion">Mary</t:persName> (?), <t:ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/CovenantMercy">Kidāna Mǝḥrat</t:ref>, <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus</t:persName>, 
                     <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS12016Evangelists#Four">Four Living Creatures</t:persName>, <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4585Georgeo">George</t:persName>, separately one tābot of <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS1251Abiyae">ʿAbiya ʾƎgziʾ</t:persName> was mentioned.</t:ab>
                  
